From df41c4381380766bba5015ed0fa9f29a6ccc47b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:51:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a 429 of magpie's own, every account held, is asked
 again in half a minute, not slept off to the window's renewal (#2526)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When every account serving a model is held at its usage cap or set not
to spend its credits, the gateway refuses the request itself (429) and
names the soonest window's renewal as Retry-After — hours off. An agent
that waits as told (Codex's responses_retry sleeps to the Retry-After)
sat a turn out for 80 minutes on one local refusal while the other
account had come back under it, and nothing told it to ask sooner
(#2526).

The wait magpie itself names is held to cappedRecheck, half a minute:
magpie reads what each account has left again about every minute, so
asked again sooner, it finds one that came back — the refusal says so
now, and a window renewing within the bound is believed as it says. The
checkpoint refusal (#2517) says the same. A refusal of the vendor's own
keeps the vendor's Retry-After, and the error-aware rest of routing
(restAfter, patience, autoReset) is unchanged.

Test: TestCodexNoCreditsRetryAfterBounded — two accounts held as they
won't spend their credits, their windows renewing hours off, get a
Retry-After of the bound, not the renewal (red before, "10800"); a
window renewing within the bound is believed as it says.

Fixes #2526
